---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const entries = [
  {
    date: "2026-11-13",
    items: [
      "Fixed the intuitive EODFDB instructions: before the final M2 the centres must be upside down, not aligned.",
      "Roux comparison: added step-by-step totals (Roux 23.1, ZBRoux 23.7) next to the optimal ones (21.4 and 22.9).",
      "Said per set how the computed algorithm lists compare with human ones, and that both algorithm averages are weighted.",
      "Added a trainer for EODFDB and ZBLL.",
    ],
  },
  {
    date: "2026-11-12",
    items: [
      "Added a computed CMLL list (42 cases), generated with the same search as ZBLL, so the Roux comparison uses like-for-like numbers.",
      "Roux comparison: turns of the top layer counted the same way on both sides; Roux about 21.4, ZBRoux about 22.9.",
      "EODFDB cases are shown from the angle where their shortest solution starts, so no algorithm begins with a turn of the top layer. 422 cases got one move shorter.",
      "Mirror pairs are shown from reflected angles; a mirror's algorithm is exactly the original with U and U' swapped.",
      "Added the 46-case EODFDB set with its definition, the Burnside derivation of the case counts, and per-case and per-position averages.",
      "Added downloadable JSON and CSV data, this changelog, and a who-should-use-it section.",
      "Licensed the algorithm data under CC BY 4.0 and the code under MIT.",
    ],
  },
  {
    date: "2026-11-11",
    items: [
      "First version: ZBRoux guide, EODFDB case finder (992 cases), ZBLL lists and finder (493 cases), LEOR EOStripe case lists and solver.",
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Changelog" description="What has changed on the ZBRoux Wiki and in its data.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Changelog</h1>
    <p class="lede">Changes to the pages and to the algorithm data, newest first. The full history is in the <a href="https://github.com/VKSFY/zbroux-wiki/commits/main">repository</a>.</p>
    {entries.map((e) => (
      <section>
        <h2>{e.date}</h2>
        <ul>{e.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </article>
</Base>
